# Zenodo 读取本文件预填归档记录的元数据（作者、标题、许可）。
# 改动本文件后需在 GitHub 上重新打 tag 才会生效。

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying results, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "Cross-centre calibration drift of acute severity scores"
abstract: >-
  Companion code, prespecified analysis plans and figures for a retrospective
  multicentre study of calibration drift in acute severity scoring. Working in 103
  intensive-care units from the eICU Collaborative Research Database, the study
  shows that a SOFA-based model's discrimination is stable across centres (AUC
  0.649-0.812) while calibration is not (observed-to-expected mortality ratio
  0.69-1.54; I-squared 75%), that the variation is not explained by measured
  case-mix and grows rather than shrinks with centre size, that it is unstable
  year to year, and that naive centre-by-centre recalibration is not the remedy
  it is usually assumed to be. Empirical-Bayes shrinkage of each centre's
  calibration offset toward the pooled mean reverses this, at a local sample size
  of 25, with shrinkage parameters that transfer to MIMIC-IV without refitting.

type: software

license: MIT

